Index: Project

Purpose:
  Project-level routing table. Root INDEX.sdd routes here for project-
  specific state. This file maps where project artifacts live and how
  they relate to each other.

  This file contains SCHEMA and ROUTING only — no concrete project data.
  Concrete project instances are generated per prompt into project/.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  PROJECT.sdd (project model entry point)
   2  INDEX.sdd   (this file — project map)
   3  templates/INDEX.sdd (reusable project templates)
   4  docs/INDEX.sdd (human docs)
   5  docs/mappings.sdd (doc-to-sdd mappings)
   6  docs/ownership.sdd (doc ownership)
   7  architecture/INDEX.sdd (project architecture map)
   8  architecture/system.sdd (system architecture)
   9  context/INDEX.sdd (project context router)
   10 context/map.sdd (project context map)
   11 context/active.sdd (active context instances)
   12 mode.sdd (project mode)
   13 decisions/INDEX.sdd (decision index)
   14 tasks/INDEX.sdd (task scheduler map)
   15 stack/INDEX.sdd (project stack selection)

Rules:
  [PI1] AI MUST resolve project context before reading any project artifact.
  [PI2] AI MUST use the task scheduler map (tasks/INDEX.sdd) to find
        ready/unblocked tasks — MUST NOT scan tasks/ blindly.
  [PI3] Task execution order is determined by dependency graph, NOT task ID.
  [PI4] A task with unresolved dependencies MUST remain in WAIT state.
  [PI5] When a task completes, AI MUST re-evaluate the dependency graph
        to unlock dependent tasks.
  [PI6] AI MUST load minimum sufficient task context — no full task catalog reads.

